            <ArticleTitle>Macrolide-Resistant Mycoplasma pneumoniae Infection, Japan, 2008-2015.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1703-1706</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3201/eid2310.170106</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We evaluated isolates obtained from children with Mycoplasma pneumoniae infection throughout Japan during 2008-2015. The highest prevalence of macrolide-resistant M. pneumoniae was 81.6% in 2012, followed by 59.3% in 2014 and 43.6% in 2015. The prevalence of macrolide-resistant M. pneumoniae among children in Japan has decreased.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
